From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 20:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Player: track optional resume callback completion

A legacy resume callback can synchronously request a seek while its player
notification was queued asynchronously. Returning from the notification
broadcast therefore does not establish that the seek callback has finished.

Add optional internal completion tracking through the application and Python
callback dispatch. Decorate only a tracked resume callback. Successful return,
exception and callback destruction each complete a ticket exactly once.
Sealed registration prevents fast recipients from finishing a broadcast early;
cancellation remains terminal even when an old callback returns later.
Unsupported callback implementations preserve their notification but cannot
certify asynchronous completion. The ordinary no-fence path stays unchanged.

Tickets publish bookkeeping only, never player calls under callback locks.
The waiting player must remain asynchronous and process a same-priority FIFO
barrier after completion, then check the current output generation. A resume
request identity survives a callback-induced seek; a media generation does not.
This patch provides completion plumbing only: VideoPlayer does not yet create
a fence, hold presentation or enable historical audio output.

The API and callback ownership are shared Kodi code; an AML-specific hook
cannot observe legacy callback return/removal here. No addon code, settings
or public Python callbacks are changed.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/xbmc/application/ApplicationPlayerCallback.cpp b/xbmc/application/ApplicationPlayerCallback.cpp
index d4ff73f208..b1d5032002 100644
--- a/xbmc/application/ApplicationPlayerCallback.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/application/ApplicationPlayerCallback.cpp
@@ -420,9 +420,15 @@ void CApplicationPlayerCallback::OnPlayBackPaused()
 }
 
 void CApplicationPlayerCallback::OnPlayBackResumed()
+{
+  OnPlayBackResumed({});
+}
+
+void CApplicationPlayerCallback::OnPlayBackResumed(
+    const std::shared_ptr<CPlaybackCallbackFence>& fence)
 {
 #ifdef HAS_PYTHON
-  CServiceBroker::GetXBPython().OnPlayBackResumed();
+  CServiceBroker::GetXBPython().OnPlayBackResumed(fence);
 #endif
 
   CGUIMessage msg(GUI_MSG_PLAYBACK_RESUMED, 0, 0);
